---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import Layout from '../../../components/Layout.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '../../../components/Breadcrumb.astro';
import { withBase } from '../../../lib/paths';
import { segmentNumbers } from '../../../lib/segments';

const segmentMetaEntries = await getCollection('segmentMeta');
const segments = segmentNumbers(segmentMetaEntries);
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<Layout title="Segments" description="Mr Casino's three-part top-down programme: Segments 1-3, given after the Weekly Programme.">
  <Breadcrumb
    items={[
      { label: 'Tasks', href: withBase('/', base) },
      { label: 'Segments' },
    ]}
  />
  <h1>Segments</h1>
  <p class="page-intro">
    Mr Casino's three-part top-down programme, given after the <a href={withBase('/tasks/weeks/', base)}>Weekly Programme</a>.
    He opened it with "#reflection - The next chapter": "Introducing with a 3×3 task segment - the bootcamp will be
    delivered over the next 3 weekends". Each Segment moves one level further down the same top-down process, from
    swing direction to the final LTF entry, and each has one assignment, paired here with my own work.
  </p>
  <p class="page-intro">
    The framework taught across the three Segments is gathered on <a href={withBase('/reference/top-down-extraction-cycle/', base)}>The Top-Down Extraction Cycle</a> (Reference).
    Segment 3 ends by pointing to a further "future (locked) final advanced segement" (<a href={withBase('/tasks/segments/3/assignment/#still-to-come', base)}>open thread</a>).
  </p>
  {segments.length === 0 && <p class="empty-state">No segments yet.</p>}
  <div class="branch-grid">
    {segments.map((segment) => {
      const meta = segmentMetaEntries.find((entry) => entry.id === segment)!;
      return (
        <a class="branch-card" href={withBase(`/tasks/segments/${segment}/`, base)}>
          <span class="card-badge">SEGMENT {segment}</span>
          <h3>{meta.data.title}</h3>
          <p>"{meta.data.purpose}"</p>
        </a>
      );
    })}
  </div>
  <p class="page-intro">
    <em>Not the same as the three fundamentals "segments" announced after Week 1: those are the <a href={withBase('/misc/fundamentals-series-geopolitical-state-of-the-world/', base)}>Fundamentals Series</a>.</em>
  </p>
</Layout>
